---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { meta } from '../../data/snapshot';

// 2026-09-24 (owner ruling): CCIR is independent market data and research.
// This page replaces /documents/governance and /documents/change-management
// (both 301 here) and the retired IOSCO self-assessment.
---
<Base
  title="How We Publish · CCIR"
  ogImage="/og/documents.png"
  description="Who publishes CCIR data, the independence it is published under, how changes to the method are versioned and disclosed, and how to question a number."
  showTape={false}
>
  <section class="wrap page-top">
    <PageHeader title="How We Publish" crumbs={[{ href: '/documents', label: 'Documents' }]} kicker="Documents" asOf={meta.as_of_date} asOfLabel="as published" display>
      <p class="standfirst">
        Who publishes the data, the independence it is published under, how
        the method can change, and how to question a number.
      </p>
    </PageHeader>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">01</span> Publisher</h2>
      <p>
        CCIR data and research are published by <strong>Compute Credit Index
        Research LLC</strong>, a Delaware limited liability company formed
        March 11, 2026. Contact:
        <a href="mailto:research@ccir.io">research@ccir.io</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">02</span> Independence</h2>
      <p>
        CCIR operates no marketplace, runs no trading desk, and holds no
        positions in the markets it measures. No revenue depends on the level
        of any published value. Data partners never buy placement, weight or
        influence over a published value. Raw contributions stay confidential,
        and only aggregates publish. CCIR measures prices. It does not value or
        rate any asset.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">03</span> Versions and Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Every published row carries a methodology version. A change to
        collection, aggregation, panel rules or series definitions increments
        the version. Values are computed automatically. Nobody adjusts a
        published value by hand.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Material changes</strong> are announced in the
        <a href="/documents/changelog">change log</a> before they take effect,
        with the reason and the expected effect. A change is material when it
        would move a headline series' 30-day average by more than 10%.</li>
        <li><strong>Defect fixes</strong> may take effect at once. The fix, its
        reason and its effect are logged.</li>
        <li><strong>Restatements</strong> republish history in full under the
        current version. Prior snapshots stay retrievable in the data
        repository's history.</li>
        <li><strong>Series breaks.</strong> When a change alters what a series
        measures, the old series ends and a new identifier begins. History is
        never redefined in place.</li>
        <li><strong>Sources</strong> enter only through a panel version change.
        A source that stops publishing carries forward at its last good price
        for up to seven days, then leaves its cells.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">04</span> Questions and Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Anyone may question a published value or the treatment of a source by
        writing to <a href="mailto:research@ccir.io">research@ccir.io</a>. We
        acknowledge substantive questions within five business days and answer
        them against the underlying observations and the published
        <a href="/documents/methodology">method</a>. Where a question finds a
        defect, the correction and its outcome go in the change log.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <style>
    .sec { margin: 26px 0; max-width: 76ch; }
    .sec h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: var(--fs-xl);
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    .sec .n {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: var(--fs-sm);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-weight: var(--weight-strong);
    }
    .sec p, .sec ul {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: var(--fs-md);
      color: var(--ink);
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .sec ul { padding-left: 20px; }
    .sec li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .sec strong { color: var(--accent); }
  </style>
</Base>
